            <div xml:id="d189">

                <pb facs="0413" n="297" sameAs="frus:frus1923v01/pg297"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.E/191b: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Chile</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Collier</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-03-08T19:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 8, 1923—7
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>30. The Chilean Ambassador called on me this morning to discuss the question of
                    Mexican participation in the approaching Pan American Conference. I have sent
                    him today the following <hi rendition="#italic">Aide-Memoire</hi> on the
                    subject:</p>
                <p>[Here follows the text of the <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi>, which is
                    the same, <hi rendition="#italic">mutatis mutandis</hi>, as the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> to the Brazilian Ambassador, quoted in
                    the Department’s telegram no. 23, March 5, to the Ambassador in Brazil, printed
                    on <ref target="#pg295">page 295</ref>.]</p>
                <p>The above is for your confidential information only and requires no action on
                    your part. Repeat to Lima, as Department’s [No.] 12, Buenos Aires as No. 8 and
                    Montevideo as No. 7.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
